-- title:
--   Good-reduction specialisation of J₀(M) above ℓ∤ M
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $M\ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid M$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $\ell$ in the project's sense that $\ell$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and assume $\kappa$ has characteristic $\ell$ and is algebraically closed. Assume further the equality of intermediate fields $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M=\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa\,M$ inside $\kappa((q))$, i.e. the subfield generated over $\kappa$ by $\mathrm{jqModC}$ and $\mathrm{jqNModC}$ coincides with the one generated by the divisor expansions; call this hypothesis $h_E$ and let $c$ be the induced isomorphism $\mathrm{Pic0}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M)\cong \mathrm{Pic0}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa\,M)$ obtained from `Pic0.congr` (here $\mathrm{Pic0}\,K\,F$ is the group of degree-zero divisors on the places of $F/K$ modulo principal ones). Give $\mathrm{JZero}\,M=\mathrm{Pic0}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,(\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M)$ the Hecke action `heckeModuleBar M` of $\mathrm{HeckeAlg}=\mathbb Z[X_q:q\text{ prime}]$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a `HeckeAlg`-module structure on $\mathrm{Pic0}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M)$ together with a datum $D$ of the project's structure `JZeroGoodReductionSpecialization_alt` for $A$, $\ell$, $M$ — that is, additive maps $\mathrm{sp}$ from $\mathrm{JZero}\,M$ to that group and $F$ on that group, with $\mathrm{sp}$ surjective and Hecke-equivariant, $\mathrm{sp}(\sigma\cdot x)=\mathrm{sp}(x)$ for $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$, $\mathrm{sp}(\sigma\cdot x)=F(\mathrm{sp}\,x)$ for every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $A$ for $\ell$, $\mathrm{sp}$ injective on $p$-power torsion for every $p$ not divisible by $\ell$, and $F$ satisfying the project's predicate `SpecialFibreRelation` for $\ell$ — such that moreover $\mathrm{sp}(x)=c^{-1}(\mathrm{reductionModL}\,A\,M\,x)$ for all $x$ and $F(y)=c^{-1}(\mathrm{frobeniusPushforwardModL}\,\kappa\,M\,\ell\,(c\,y))$ for all $y$.
--
--   This packages the reduction of divisor classes of the modular function field modulo a place above $\ell\nmid M$, in the style of Deuring, into the single datum of a good-reduction specialisation of $J_0(M)$: a surjective Hecke-equivariant reduction map, trivial on inertia, intertwining Frobenius with the Frobenius push-forward on the special fibre, injective on prime-to-$\ell$ torsion, and satisfying the Eichler–Shimura-type relation on the special fibre. It is the input to the construction, for a newform of level dividing $M$, of the Galois representation on the relevant Tate module together with its local behaviour at primes not dividing the level.
